<article class="env-lemma" id="01KT">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01KT">Lemma <span data-tag="01KT">26.21.11</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. Let $s : S \to X$ be a section of $f$ (in a formula $f \circ s = \text{id}_ S$). Then $s$ is an immersion. If $f$ is separated then $s$ is a closed immersion. If $f$ is quasi-separated, then $s$ is quasi-compact. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is a special case of Lemma <a href="/tag/01KS" data-tag="01KS">26.21.10</a> applied to $g =s$ so the morphism $i = s : S \to S \times _ S X$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>